  "notes": [
    "source: the source key a door reads from the file's sources; tags: the resource's tags as the export spells them; map: the user's own map for this run (tag to type), when the case has one; template: true for a resource in the tool's templates folder.",
    "file: the import map value a door read, in place of import-map.json beside this page, when the case has one. A file whose version is not the number 1 is not an import map: the door reads no table, never an error, and every case on such a file is typed as if the file were not there. A declined offer reads the same way.",
    "type: the type a door that applied the table (on the user's yes) gives the resource, or null: untyped (the Python package's Narrative with supertype Article). why: the strongest way that named the type (user map, then tag, then table), or why none: ambiguous (two distinct types named), no type (every tag a no_type word), template (a template left untyped that carries a tag the table has), untyped (anything else).",
    "offered: the tags of an untyped resource that a door lists as ones a map could type: folded (trimmed, lower-cased), once each, sorted, without the no_type words of a table it read; empty on a typed resource."
  ],
